---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Amelia Rowland"
  description="Amelia Rowland is a GIS specialist, cartographer, and graduate student in Geography: Global Change and Sustainability at the University of Vienna."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-16 pb-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">About</h1>

    <div class="prose-map mt-8">
      <p>
        Hi! I'm Amelia — a consultant, GIS specialist, and software product engineer
        inspired by sustainability, systems thinking, and telling stories with data.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm currently completing a Master's in Geography: Global Change and
        Sustainability at the University of Vienna, specializing in socio-economic
        transformations. This work has deepened my understanding of the complexity
        behind sustainability challenges and the systems-level thinking needed to
        address them. I'm excited to keep contributing and collaborating on work
        related to sustainable urban development.
      </p>

      <h2>Background</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Product Engineer, Esri</strong> — As a Product Engineer at Esri 
         for the Location Analytics and ArcGIS Enterprise teams, I served as a bridge 
         between product users and software engineers. Through this work I collaborated
         with front-end and back-end teams to investigate and resolve technical issues, 
         test solutions, support documentation, and improve the user experience. I also 
         engaged with current and prospective customers at the Esri Developer & Technology 
         Summit, demonstrating product value and gathering insights into user needs and 
         priorities.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GIS Specialist, VHB</strong> — At VHB I provided GIS expertise on a 
        variety of projects including transportation, water resources, and environmental 
        regulation. Through these projects I collaborated with planners, environmental 
        scientists, project managers, and other analysts to deliver interactive web app 
        experiences, create and analyze data, process field maps, and optimize workflows.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GIS Analyst, Jacobs</strong> — As a GIS Analyst at Jacobs I worked on 
        environmental and city planning consulting projects. Primarily used ArcMap, 
        ArcGIS Pro, and ArcGIS Online. Gained coding experience using Python/model 
        builder in ArcMap and Jupyter Notebook.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Education</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>MSc Geography: Global Change and Sustainability, University of Vienna</strong> —
          In this program I am specializing in socio-economic Transformations and currently 
          finalizing my thesis "Renewable Innovation and Local Opposition: A Regional 
          Perspective on the U.S. Energy Transition". Coursework included (but is not limited to):
          <ul>
            <li>Geography of Innovation and Sustainability Transformations</li>
            <li>Spatial Data Science</li>
            <li>Socio-Economic Transformation in Space: Innovative Approaches for Circular Economy</li>
            <li>Inter- and Transdisciplinary Approaches to Global Change and Sustainability</li>
            <li>Economic Psychology</li>
            <li>Seminar in Human Geography: Urban Complexity and Systems Thinking</li>
            <li>Development Policy and Development Cooperation Architecture</li>
            <li>Pathways to Sustainability: Knowledge, Action and Policy Landscapes</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>BS Geographic Information Science and Cartography, minor in Humanitarian
          Affairs, James Madison University</strong> — Concentrations include Applied GIS (AGIS), 
          Environmental Conservation, Sustainability and Development (ECSD)
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Toolbox</h2>
      <p>QGIS · ArcGIS Pro · ArcGIS Online · Python · Data management · Leaflet · Jupyter Notebook · Codex</p>

      <p>
        Find me on
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ameliarowland09/" target="_blank" rel="noopener me">LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
